{
  "name": "306. xAI batch lifecycle: inline chat lines, retrieve, list, paged results, cancel; files and a file batch (xai batch lifecycle)",
  "description": "Pins xAI batches on the unified /v1/batches routes (TXE-6664, Bifrost-Tokun contract C8). Create takes inline OpenAI-shape chat lines and reaches xAI as two calls: POST /v1/batches with a name that carries the batch's metadata (tokun_batch_id=...), then POST /v1/batches/{id}/requests with one batch_request per line whose batch_request_id is the line's custom_id. Retrieve maps xAI's state counters to request_counts and a unified status; list returns the team's batches with the metadata read back from their names (the recovery path when a create response is lost); results page through /v1/batches/{id}/results with after/limit, each line carrying custom_id, status, and either an OpenAI chat response.body with the unified usage plus usage.vendor_cost in usd_ticks, or the vendor's error; cancel calls :cancel. Every lifecycle call names the key with x-bf-api-key (the profile's xAI key has use_for_batch_api: true). The [EXPECT-400] row is free: a non-chat line is refused before any upstream call. It names no key, so it also runs against the provider error fixture profile, whose xAI key is a batch key too. The lifecycle rows submit a real batch (xAI bills batch tokens at 20% off), so they are [PREVIEW]: they run only with INCLUDE_PREVIEW=1. Results may still be empty when the row runs, since xAI processes batches asynchronously; the row asserts the paging shape always and the line shape for every line returned. The file rows upload tests/e2e/api/fixtures/xai-batch-input.jsonl to /v1/files with purpose batch (sent to xAI, which stores it), retrieve, list and read it back, create a batch from it by input_file_id and cancel that batch, then delete the file; they are [PREVIEW] too, because the file batch is a real batch.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "[EXPECT-400] /v1/batches - xai refuses a non-chat line before any upstream call - xai/grok-4.3 - xai batch lifecycle",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('a non-chat line is refused as an unsupported parameter', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'unexpected status: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(400);",
              "  var j = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect((j.extra_fields || {}).error_type, 'error_type: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('caller_unsupported_parameter');",
              "  pm.expect((j.error || {}).message, 'message: ' + pm.response.text()).to.include('/v1/chat/completions');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"xai/grok-4.3\",\n  \"endpoint\": \"/v1/embeddings\",\n  \"completion_window\": \"24h\",\n  \"requests\": [\n    {\n      \"custom_id\": \"line-1\",\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"url\": \"/v1/embeddings\",\n      \"body\": {\n        \"model\": \"grok-4.3\",\n        \"input\": \"hello\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/batches",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "batches"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
